---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/i18n';

export const prerender = true;

Astro.locals.locale = 'en';

const favoritesUrl = href('/favoritos', 'en');
---

<Legal title="Cookie policy" updated="August 2026">
  <p>
    This website does not show cookie banners because there is nothing to accept: <strong>we use no cookies or equivalent
    technologies for analytics, advertising, audience measurement or tracking</strong>. The only storage we use is strictly
    necessary for the website to work, and is therefore exempt from consent under Article 22.2 of Spanish Law 34/2002 (LSSI-CE) and the criteria of the Spanish DPA
    and the GTICO.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Storage used by this site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Theme preference</strong> — <code>localStorage: madmovil:theme</code>. Stores whether you prefer
      the light or dark theme. Only your browser reads it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Language preference</strong> — <code>localStorage: madmovil:locale</code>. Remembers the language
      chosen in the selector (the language of each page is determined by its URL, not by this value).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Favourites</strong> — <code>localStorage: madmovil:favorites</code>. Your favourite stops are
      stored only on your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Favourites sync (optional)</strong> — <code>localStorage/sessionStorage: madmovil:vault</code> and <code>madmovil:vault-status</code>. If you
      enable sync, the sync code is stored only if you tick
      “remember on this device”; otherwise it lives in session storage and is deleted when the browser closes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Query caches</strong> — <code>localStorage: madmovil:stopnames</code>, <code>madmovil:stopaddresses</code>, <code>madmovil:stoplines</code> and
      their counterparts (<code>crtm*</code>, <code>linecolors</code>). Local copies of public data (stop names, addresses and
      lines, line colours) to avoid repeating requests. They contain no personal data.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    All of the above is installed only when you need it as a user (theme, language, favourites or sync) and is
    not used to track or identify you across sites.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How to delete this data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      From your browser: “Clear browsing data” → cookies and other site data. You can also delete <code>madmovil.es</code> data
      individually in the site settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      Favourites are removed from the site itself (the star on each stop or the <a href={favoritesUrl}>Favourites</a> page), and the
      remote sync copy with the “Delete remote copy” button.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Future changes</h2>
  <p>
    If in the future we added any cookie or storage that is not strictly necessary (for example, aggregate
    statistics), we would ask for your prior consent through a banner with clear options and would update this
    policy.
  </p>
</Legal>
